    "statement": "Grooves on intertidal artificial structures supported macroalgae, mobile and non-mobile invertebrate species that were absent from structure surfaces without grooves.",
    "citations": [
      "3473"
    ]
  },
  {
    "statement": "Grooves supported higher species richness than small ridges or ledges created between the grooves.",
    "citations": [
      "3473"
    ]
  },
  {
    "statement": "Grooves did not consistently increase combined macroalgae and invertebrate community composition or abundance on structure surfaces.",
    "citations": [
      "3473"
    ]
  },
  {
    "statement": "Transplanting or seeding organisms onto intertidal artificial structures was examined in seven Australian estuarine studies.",
    "citations": [
      "3472"
    ]
  },
  {
    "statement": "Transplanted oysters on intertidal artificial structures supported macroalgae, mobile invertebrate, non-mobile invertebrate and fish species that were absent from structure surfaces without transplanted oysters.",
    "citations": [
      "3472"
    ]
  },
  {
    "statement": "Transplanting oysters had mixed effects on combined macroalgae and invertebrate species richness and diversity, depending on site and presence of grooves and small ridges on surfaces.",
    "citations": [
      "3472"
    ]
  },
  {
    "statement": "Transplanting oysters increased mobile invertebrate species richness.",
    "citations": [
      "3472"
    ]
  },
  {
    "statement": "Creating short flexible habitats on intertidal artificial structures was studied in one Australian estuarine site.",
    "citations": [
      "3459"
    ]
  },
  {
    "statement": "Creating short flexible habitats on intertidal artificial structures altered the combined macroalgae and non-mobile invertebrate community composition.",
    "citations": [
      "3459"
    ]
  },
  {
    "statement": "Creating short flexible habitats on intertidal artificial structures decreased combined macroalgae, invertebrate and fish species richness during low tide.",
    "citations": [
      "3459"
    ]
  },
  {
    "statement": "Using environmentally-sensitive materials on both intertidal and subtidal artificial structures has been studied in Australian estuaries.",
    "citations": [
      "3469",
      "3470"
    ]
  },
  {
    "statement": "Using sandstone in place of basalt on artificial structures had mixed effects on community composition depending on site.",
    "citations": [
      "3469",
      "3470"
    ]
  },
  {
    "statement": "Reduced-pH-concrete surfaces on artificial structures supported species absent from standard-concrete surfaces.",
    "citations": [
      "3469",
      "3470"
    ]
  },
  {
    "statement": "Reducing the slope of intertidal artificial structures was examined in Australian estuarine studies.",
    "citations": [
      "3461"
    ]
  },
  {
